-- title:
--   Kernel of the q-expansion map is a minimal prime
-- statement:
--   Let $q\ge 5$ and $\ell\ge 3$ be distinct primes, $M'\ge 1$ with $q\nmid M'$ and $\ell\nmid M'$, let $L$ be a field of characteristic $0$ containing a primitive $(q\ell)$-th root of unity $\xi$ for which some ring homomorphism $L\to\mathbb C$ sends $\xi$ to $\exp(2\pi i/(q\ell))$, and let $K\subseteq L(\!(\mathsf q)\!)$ be the subfield generated over $L$ by the coefficientwise image of the $q$-expansion function field of $X_H$ of level $(q\ell)^2M'$, where $H$ is the kernel of the reduction $(\mathbb Z/(q\ell)^2M')^\times\to(\mathbb Z/q\ell)^\times$. Let $A$ be a discrete valuation ring with fraction field $L$ and $q$ in its maximal ideal, with $K$ an $A$-algebra through $L$, and let $j\in K$, $j\neq 0$, be the $q$-expansion of the modular $j$-function. Assume $\ell$ and $M'$ are units in $A$, assume level-$\ell$ structures and $\Gamma_0(p^k)$-generator-kernel polynomials transform correctly under Weierstrass variable changes, and fix $A$-data consisting of a chord-tangent family $\mathcal G$ of relative group laws with identity section in the origin chart, a level transport $\mathcal T$ at $q$ compatible with sections, and graded homomorphisms realising variable changes and coefficient maps on the projective models. Let $P_0$ be a fine moduli package for the resulting moduli datum (an $A$-algebra $B_0$, of finite type over $A$, carrying a universal object through which every $T$-point factors uniquely), $\iota:B_0\to K$ an $A$-algebra map whose values generate $K$ as a field of fractions (every $k\in K$ is $\iota x/\iota y$ with $\iota y\neq 0$), and suppose $B_0$ is integral over the $A$-subalgebra generated by `P₀.j₀`. Then $\ker\iota$ is a minimal prime ideal of $B_0$, i.e. it lies in the minimal primes over $(0)$.
--
--   This is the dimension-theoretic step identifying the kernel of the $q$-expansion map on the full-level fine moduli ring as a minimal prime, so that the moduli ring has a component whose function field is the modular function field $K$. It is used to show that $K$ is integral over the image of $\iota$, en route to comparing the fine moduli ring with the modular curve of level $(q\ell)^2M'$.
-- source:
--   https://github.com/anthropics/fermats-last-theorem/blob/aa2d8b34692b16c70f699536de0d8e75b9a3e9ef/Theorems/Thm_ModularCurve_FullLevel_ker_mem_minimalPrimes_of_levelModuliPackageAbs_qExpansion_of_dense_of_exists_ringHom_gamma0Pow.lean

